CAT = "nzreConduct"; SEG = "CON"
Q = [
("Under the Code of Conduct, how often must a licensee exercise skill, care, competence and diligence?",
 "At all times in agency work", ["Only when a client complains", "Only for written agreements", "Only during open homes and auctions"],
 "Rule 5.1 of the Professional Conduct and Client Care Rules 2012 requires skill, care, competence and diligence at all times when carrying out real estate agency work."),
("What does rule 5.2 expect a licensee to know?",
 "The Act, rules and relevant law", ["Only the Act and its sections", "Only the rules the agency wrote", "Only the law about residential sales"],
 "Rule 5.2 requires a sound knowledge of the Act, regulations, rules issued by the Authority and other legislation relevant to real estate agency work."),
("A licensee owes fiduciary obligations to whom?",
 "The licensee's client", ["Every customer equally", "The agency's other listings", "The Authority"],
 "Rule 6.1 requires a licensee to comply with fiduciary obligations to the client. Rule 6.2 separately requires fair dealing with all parties."),
("In a sale, the licensee works for the vendor. How must the licensee treat a buyer?",
 "Fairly and in good faith", ["As a stranger owed nothing", "As a second client with equal duties", "As an opponent to be outmanoeuvred"],
 "Rule 6.2 requires a licensee to act in good faith and deal fairly with all parties to a transaction, even though the fiduciary duty is to the client."),
("Which conduct falls squarely under rule 6.3?",
 "Conduct damaging the industry", ["Charging a high commission rate", "Taking time off in the week", "Working for a rival agency firm"],
 "Rule 6.3 says a licensee must not engage in conduct likely to bring the industry into disrepute."),
("A buyer asks if the vendor has had other offers. The licensee knows of none but says there are three. This breaches:",
 "The ban on misleading customers", ["Only the agency's own policy", "The rule on advertising", "No rule, it is a negotiating tactic"],
 "Rule 6.4 bars misleading a customer or client, giving false information, or withholding information that should be provided by law or in fairness."),
("A licensee has reasonable grounds to suspect another licensee of misconduct. The licensee:",
 "Must report to the Authority", ["May wait for a complaint first", "Should tell the vendor instead", "Should wait for the agent to decide"],
 "Rule 7.2 says a licensee with reasonable grounds to suspect misconduct by another licensee must make a report to the Authority."),
("A licensee suspects another licensee of unsatisfactory conduct, a lesser matter than misconduct. The rules say the licensee:",
 "May make a report", ["Must make a report", "Must keep silent", "Must tell the vendors involved"],
 "Rule 7.1 says a licensee who has reasonable grounds to suspect unsatisfactory conduct may report it. Reporting is compulsory only for suspected misconduct (rule 7.2)."),
("A licensee threatens to lodge a complaint against a rival unless the rival drops a competing listing. What does the rule on complaints say?",
 "The process must not be misused", ["Complaints can be used as leverage", "Threats are fine if the claim is true", "Only agents are bound by the rule"],
 "Rule 7.3 says a licensee must not use, or threaten to use, the complaints or disciplinary process for an improper purpose."),
("A salesperson learns that a neighbour's agency work is being done by an unlicensed person. What must the salesperson do?",
 "Report it to the Authority at once", ["Wait to see whether it continues", "Tell the vendor first", "Ask the person to apply for a licence"],
 "Rule 7.4 says a licensee who learns that someone is committing an offence by doing agency work without a licence must immediately report it to the Authority."),
("An agent operates as a business. Where must the Code of Conduct rules be displayed?",
 "In each office and on websites", ["Only in the agent's filing cabinet", "On each new listing sheet", "On request to the agent only"],
 "Rule 8.1 requires an agent operating as a business to display the rules prominently in the public area of each office or branch and provide access to them on every website kept for the business."),
("A member of the public asks a salesperson for a copy of the Code of Conduct rules. The salesperson:",
 "Must make them available", ["Can refuse if not a client", "Must send the person to the agent", "Can charge a fee for them"],
 "Rule 8.2 requires any licensee to make the rules available to any person on request."),
("Under rule 8.3, an agent operating as a business must ensure salespersons are:",
 "Properly supervised and managed", ["Paid a share of commission", "Kept off the busy listings", "Employed rather than contracted"],
 "Rule 8.3 requires an agent operating as a business to ensure all salespersons employed or engaged are properly supervised and managed, which links to section 50 of the Act."),
("Which general duty does rule 9.1 place on a licensee?",
 "Act in the client's best interests", ["Follow every instruction, even if unlawful", "Maximise the commission", "Keep the vendor's costs hidden"],
 "Rule 9.1 requires a licensee to act in the best interests of a client and follow the client's instructions unless to do so would be contrary to law."),
("A licensee tells a buyer the offer \"expires in an hour\" to push a quick decision when nothing has changed. Which rule is in play?",
 "No undue or unfair pressure", ["No advertising without consent", "Safeguarding keys", "Recording a buyer's offer"],
 "Rule 9.2 says a licensee must not engage in conduct that would put a prospective client, client or customer under undue or unfair pressure."),
("A vendor wants to hear only when something big happens. What does rule 9.3 say?",
 "Update them unless told otherwise", ["Contact them daily without exception", "Contact them only at settlement", "Contact only their solicitor"],
 "Rule 9.3 requires regular, timely communication that keeps the client well informed, unless the client instructs otherwise."),
("Before an open home, what must a licensee take due care about under rule 9.5?",
 "Land security and damage risks", ["The licensee's own parking spot", "The cost of the refreshments", "The number of visitors expected"],
 "Rule 9.5 requires due care to ensure the security of the land or business and to avoid risks of damage from customers, or clients who are not the owner, accessing it."),
("Under rule 9.8, a licensee notices a customer clearly cannot follow a contract. The licensee must not:",
 "Exploit that difficulty", ["Offer to explain the clauses", "Suggest legal advice", "Allow more time to decide"],
 "Rule 9.8 says a licensee must not take advantage of a person's inability to understand relevant documents where that inability is reasonably apparent."),
("A salesperson would earn two commissions on the same sale by acting in two roles. The rules say the licensee:",
 "Must not act in that capacity", ["May do so if disclosed", "May do so with the agent's consent", "May do so for a rural sale"],
 "Rule 9.14 says a licensee must not act in a capacity that would attract more than one commission in the same transaction."),
("A licensee runs a side business that could get in the way of looking after clients. What does rule 9.15 say?",
 "It must not harm client duties", ["It is a private matter alone", "It is acceptable if profitable", "It must be run by a family member"],
 "Rule 9.15 bars business or professional activity outside agency work where it would, or could reasonably be expected to, compromise the licensee's obligations."),
("A salesperson learns a vendor's lowest acceptable price and uses the figure to help a relative buy. This is:",
 "Misuse of client confidences", ["Normal practice for staff", "A permitted family discount", "Not covered by any of the rules"],
 "Rule 9.16 says a licensee must not use information that is confidential to a client for the benefit of any other person or of the licensee."),
("A licensee wishes to pass on a client's confidential personal information to a third party. Which basis is clearly allowed?",
 "The client's written consent", ["The agent's request", "The buyer's polite request", "The licensee's belief it helps"],
 "Rule 9.17 allows disclosure with the client's written consent, or where needed to answer a complaint, required by law, or consistent with privacy principles, and only to the extent necessary."),
("Do the Code of Conduct rules set the most a licensee must do or the least?",
 "The minimum standards", ["The ideal standard", "A full list of every duty", "Standards for agents only"],
 "Rule 3.3 says the rules are minimum standards and a reference point for discipline, and a charge can be brought even if it is not based on a breach of a specific rule."),
("A complaint alleges poor conduct that is not covered by any specific numbered rule. What follows?",
 "A charge may still be brought", ["It must be dismissed", "It goes to the Commerce Commission", "Only a civil court can hear it"],
 "Rule 3.3 says a charge of misconduct or unsatisfactory conduct may be brought despite not being based on a breach of any specific rule."),
]
